 reads its stdin JSON and prints a `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` whose first line starts `Advisor: live` for a prompt that holds `live` and `Advisor: stale` otherwise, each followed by a second line. Case one runs `node <MBC> --root <tmp>` and expects exit 0, `liveRows` 1, two `rows`, the `cost-stale` row with `live` false and `medianHeadBytes` and `medianBytes` equal to the UTF-8 lengths of the live head and the live context. Case two runs `--rows cost-stale` on the same root and expects exit 2 and stdout `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",\"rows\":1,\"liveRows\":0}`. Remove the root after each case. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `V tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts` reports 2 passed and `node $MBC --rows not-a-row` prints `{\"error\":\"unknown_row\",\"id\":\"not-a-row\"}` and exits 2.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '84p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md | cut -c1201-2300\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794564328031,"end":1794564328280}}}}
